{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity` (the operator-run parity harness) printed the following in a fresh worktree created by `make worktree` (2026-11-09, origin/main 872e7f6c3fd):\n\n```\nError: cannot list '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker': [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker'\n```\n\nThe run continued and made model calls (see the 2026-11-09 correction comment). The message went away once any `rebar` CLI command had run in that worktree, because the CLI creates the `.tickets-tracker` symlink.\n\n## What is established (2026-11-17 PST, origin/main 83ca81e709e, worktree with no `.tickets-tracker`)\n- The harness's tracker reads depend on whether an earlier CLI call attached the store. The model-facing `show_ticket` tool every eval agent gets (`rebar_tools`, `src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py:263-289`) calls `_reads.show_ticket(ref, repo_root=repo_path)`. Called directly in this worktree with a full id, an 8-digit short id, an alias and a `rebar:` token, it returns `Error: ticket system not initialized. Run 'ticket init' first.` for every one of them. So in an unattached worktree, every eval case whose prompt says to retrieve a ticket with `show_ticket` (for example E4 and G1G2) gets an error instead of the ticket, and the measured verdicts depend on worktree state.\n- The exact \"cannot list\" line is printed by `rebar._ids._scan_tracker_root` / `_scan_alias` (`src/rebar/_ids.py:268-272`, `:452-456`) when `os.listdir(tracker_dir)` fails.\n- That line did not reproduce at 83ca81e709e. A print hook that dumps a stack on any \"cannot list\" line saw none across 27 real harness items: 1 full `main --slot standard --limit 1 --epochs 1` run (both arms), 1 `run_arm` over each of the 16 distinct plan-review criterion solvers, and 1 `run_arm` over each of the 10 distinct code-review solvers, all with `--concurrency 4`-equivalent threading. So the specific emitter on 872e7f6c3fd's path is not identified. That is not needed for the fix below, because the fix removes the missing-tracker state that every such read hits.\n- Why the CLI does not hit it: the CLI dispatcher calls `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` (`src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:387`, defined at `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py:149-178`) before any command. In a linked worktree that function symlinks the main repo's tracker (`init_core` → `_init_via_symlink`, `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:541-598`), never creates a first store, and never raises. The `python -m` harnesses do not go through the dispatcher.\n- The sibling harness `python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` has the same gap. Its run path calls `rebar.llm.review_plan` and `rebar.show_ticket` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:229`, `:254`) against the harness checkout's tracker.\n\n## Approach\nGive both operator harnesses the same store-mount step the CLI uses, at the point where a real run starts. In each `main()`, after the `--dry-run` (and, in provider_parity, `--probe`) early returns and before any model call, call `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()`. Dry-run and probe stay side-effect-free.\n- This reuses the CLI's own consent-free attach rules unchanged: it mounts an existing store by symlink or branch attach, never creates a first store, and never raises.\n- No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py`: in `main` (`:583`), call `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` after the `--probe` and `--dry-run` returns and before `run_slot`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`: in `main` (`:441`), call it after the `--dry-run` return and before `run(...)`.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` and `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py`: tests that monkeypatch `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` with a recorder and stub the run (`run_slot` / `run`) to record call order.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a non-dry-run `main` records the mount call before the first run call, for both harnesses.\n- Edge path: `--dry-run` records no mount call (both harnesses), and `--probe` records none (provider_parity).\n- Existing tests in both test modules still pass.\n- Manual check, recorded on this ticket: in a fresh `make worktree` checkout, the `show_ticket` tool returns \"ticket system not initialized\". After provider_parity's `main` has run with a stubbed `run_slot`, `.tickets-tracker` is a symlink to the main store and the same tool call returns the ticket's JSON.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both harnesses mount the existing tracker the way the CLI does before a real run, and not on `--dry-run`/`--probe`. Checked by the new unit tests.\n- [ ] In a fresh worktree, the manual check above shows the symlink created and `show_ticket` returning the ticket, recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the change."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794940506315571015,"uuid":"458e201f-1f5f-4018-9af0-a37332930fc5"}